scion: dynarmic compiles guest code about twice as fast (CPU time of short arm64 programs -47%):
- fastmem fallbacks (6048 thunks, 1.9 MB) are generated on first use into a reserved area instead of by every JIT
- the fast dispatch table has 64K entries instead of 1M (16 MB written twice and resident per JIT)
- the A64 decode table is built without copying every matcher's std::function 4096 times
- register allocation: only the locations an instruction touched are released, no candidate vector copy, no
  release-mode full scans in assertions, hot HostLocInfo accessors inline
- no perf-map names are formatted unless PERF_BUILDID_DIR is set; VerificationPass in debug builds only

